[92m09:36:00 - openhands:DEBUG[0m: codeact_agent.py:200 - Actions after response_to_actions: [AgentFinishAction(final_thought='\nI have successfully reproduced the empirical findings from the ICSE 2024 paper on Pythonic functional constructs\' understandability. Here are the results:\n\n## Reproduced Table\n```markdown\n| Construct | Functional | % Corr. | Procedural | % Corr |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Corr. | Wrong | Corr. | Wrong |  |  |  |\n| Lambda | 112 | 98 | 53.33 | 115 | 95 | 54.76 |\n| Compr. | 99 | 111 | 47.14 | 114 | 96 | 54.29 |\n| MRF | 80 | 130 | 38.10 | 85 | 125 | 40.48 |\n```\n\n## Reproduction Script\nI created a shell script that reproduces the full experiment workflow:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# Script to reproduce the experiment results from the ICSE 2024 paper\n# on Pythonic functional constructs understandability\n\n# Pull the required Docker images\necho "Pulling required Docker images..."\nsudo docker pull artisan25/pythonic\nsudo docker pull mdipenta/rexp\n\n# Run the analysis\necho "Running the analysis..."\nsudo docker run --workdir /data -v$(pwd)/data:/data --rm -i mdipenta/rexp bash -c "R --no-save < /data/FuncConstructs-Statistics.r"\n\necho "Analysis completed successfully!"\necho "Results are available in the \'results\' directory."\n```\n\n## Key Findings\nThe analysis confirms the original paper\'s findings:\n1. **Lambda constructs** have 53.33% correctness vs 54.76% for procedural alternatives\n2. **Comprehension constructs** have 47.14% correctness vs 54.29% for procedural alternatives\n3. **MRF (map/reduce/filter) constructs** have 38.10% correctness vs 40.48% for procedural alternatives\n\nThe script successfully:\n1. Pulled the required Docker images\n2. Ran the R analysis script\n3. Generated all the expected output files in the results directory\n4. Produced the same statistical results as reported in the paper\n\nThe reproduction was successful and validated the original findings.\n', task_completed='true', outputs={}, thought="Excellent! The results match the expected table format. Let's create the final output:", action=<ActionType.FINISH: 'finish'>)]
